=== PARITY (web source reproduced end-to-end) ===
  SettingsSearch.tsx is a controlled <Input type=search> driving a popover listbox of
  ranked settings; selecting a row navigate()s to its href and scrolls to the #anchor.
  Its matching is DELEGATED to searchIndex.ts (getSettingsIndex + searchSettings +
  fuzzyMatch), so BOTH files are the spec and both are ported 1:1.

  Web symbol                       → Native port
  -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  fuzzyMatch(needle, haystack)     → SettingsSearchProjector.fuzzyMatch — verbatim
                                     case-insensitive subsequence (empty needle false).
  searchSettings(index, q)         → SettingsSearchProjector.rank — q = query.trim()
                                     .lowercased(); score ladder reproduced EXACTLY
                                     (title==q 1000 ▸ prefix 800 ▸ substring 600 ▸
                                     keyword 400 ▸ desc 300 ▸ fuzzy-title 200 ▸
                                     fuzzy-desc 100); STABLE descending sort (ties keep
                                     catalog order, via (score desc, original-index asc),
                                     matching JS Array.sort stability).
  MAX_RESULTS = 8 (.slice(0, 8))   → SettingsSearchProjector.maxResults; applied in project().
  getSettingsIndex(t) [53 entries] → SettingsCatalog.entries(localize:) — same ids, hrefs,
                                     sections, titles, descriptions, keywords, AND ORDER
                                     (tesla → region → general → notifications → quiet-hours
                                     → appearance → security → privacy → advanced/backup →
                                     webhooks → reset → helix).
  navigate(entry.href) + split('#')→ SettingsDestination.from(href:) → path + optional
                                     #fragment; the view forwards it host-free via onNavigate
                                     (the host routes + scrolls to the section anchor).
  useTranslation('settings')       → P1/S10 facade SettingsSearchStrings (table
                                     "SettingsSearch"); zero English literals in Swift.
  useNavigate                      → injected onNavigate(SettingsDestination) seam.
  useId (listbox a11y wiring)      → native accessibility (combobox field label +
                                     per-row VoiceOver labels + result-area summary).

  i18n keys (acceptance: every source key has a catalog match):
    settings.search.placeholder = "Search settings…"   (field prompt)
    settings.search.label       = "Search settings"    (field a11y label)
    settings.search.noResults   = "No matching settings."   (empty state)
    + all 53 search.entries.<id>.title/.desc keys, verbatim web English fallbacks.

  FAITHFUL DIVERGENCE (no silent drift, Honesty rule 9): the web combobox uses a manual
  roving-tabindex highlight (activeIndex + ArrowUp/Down/Enter/Escape) — a DOM keyboard
  pattern. The native surface renders the matches as real focusable SwiftUI Buttons (Full
